WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.810
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS!

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.250
Cyberse Wizard's effect!

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.860
Decode Talker can now deal piercing damage!

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.170
Decode End!

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.680
You have no right to call yourself a duelist!

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.300
Playmaker saved LINK VRAINS!

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.080
Well done, Yusaku.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.580
Playmaker...

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.530
What are the true identities 
of the Knights of Hanoi?

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.410
I'll never tell you.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.000
I'll take you down with me.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.600
Oh no!  He wants to destroy us!

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:19.280
What did you do?

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.960
Protect you.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.450
If I didn't, you would've taken damage.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:25.930
And your real self would be in trouble.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.480
Anyway, you should log out.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.640
I found you, Playmaker!

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:35.380
Duel me!

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.850
Your actions were quite flashy!

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.310
Get ready!

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.320
Sorry, but I'm not interested.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:56.700
He fled.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:05.520
You seem quite tired.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.600
Yeah.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.640
After I take a break, I'll 
thoroughly analyze your program.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.840
Fiiiiiiine!

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.800
Playmaker and Ignis have teamed up.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:23.320
I never expected Playmaker 
to be the dark horse.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:26.760
Revolver, you made some wrong decisions.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.470
But there's a silver lining.  SOL 
Technologies didn't get Ignis.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.530
It won't take long to uncover his identity.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:41.240
One: He hates us - the Knights of Hanoi.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:44.950
Two: Not many people have Cyberse cards.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:52.490
Three: He'll come to me because 
he wants to battle me.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.480
You're correct.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:59.960
Let's start preparing for that fight.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.710
I run Across the universe

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:20.880
At the speed of light

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.750
Begin Loading

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:26.480
Open the door of dreams

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.050
VRAINS spreads

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:33.160
Believe in myself

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.690
VRAINS continues

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:42.000
The circuit draws the future

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:46.070
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:47.670
Access!

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.370
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:51.980
I'm now With the Wind

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:54.280
Link with my soul

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.050
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:03:57.260 --> 00:03:58.780
Now Win the Race

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.620
Connected world

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:05.120
No matter when

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:08.490
Nothing is impossible

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:12.630
Strive for hope

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:17.200
And ride the wind!

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:36.700
Who is Playmaker?

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:40.460
"Playmaker" is a person who calls the shots.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:43.700
And he calls the shots in LINK VRAINS.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:48.180
Eyewitnesses have seen him 
fight the Knights of Hanoi.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.440
It's cool that he won't reveal his identity.

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.880
If it was me, I would!

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:56.860
Playmaker is totally my type!

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.680
He's super cool and makes my heart flutter!

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:04.220
Really?  He's just an avatar.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:06.660
He can look like anyone in real life.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:10.910
Maybe he hasn't revealed himself 
because he's super ugly!

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.360
Why'd you look at me when you said that!

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:18.850
Argh...

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:22.020
Yamamoto!  So this is where you were!

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.610
Never say my name!

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:26.110
Anyway, how is it?

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:29.320
LINK VRAINS is extremely crowded.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:32.080
Usually, only duelists are here.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.700
But it's full of press today.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:37.320
Everyone is looking for Playmaker.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:40.090
Every station is on the lookout.

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:44.540
They're slowing down the network, 
so I almost crashed into buildings.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:49.040
If you turn off chat in your 
settings, it might get better.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.780
What?  I didn't know that.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.390
Hey!  You're right!

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:55.540
Playmaker has appeared!

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:56.820
Where?

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:00.410
Hi!  I'm Playmaker!

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:03.200
Hurry up and roll the camera!

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.350
Huh?  He's over there too.

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:11.550
Me is Playmaker!

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:14.590
No no, I'm Playmaker!

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.380
Very doubtful.

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:19.570
That's a lot of static.

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.840
They're probably all fakes!

00:06:22.840 --> 00:06:26.830
Sheesh.  They're all copy avatars.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:31.560
Unbelievable.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:36.960
Just by inputting the card data you 
acquired, it's creating the real thing.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:41.000
The Data Storm may be more 
incredible than we think.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:45.420
Playmaker, you're famous.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:50.430
You can erase your login, but 
you can't erase the footage.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.660
You wanted to stay low-key, but too bad.

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:55.260
How did you know?

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.920
Of course I know.

00:06:56.920 --> 00:07:01.280
I was fleeing through the 
network, so I know a lot.

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:03.270
Then what's a Data Storm?

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:08.240
I don't know.  Most of my memories were 
eaten up until only my eyeball was left.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:11.650
Whatever.  I didn't expect 
you to answer me seriously.

00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:13.480
I'll analyze you now.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.240
You're really going to analyze me?

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.190
You won't find anything.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:19.820
I can't trust you.

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:25.200
What?  Does this mean you'll learn 
all my deepest, darkest secrets?

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:26.960
How embarrassing!

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:29.860
- Kusanagi, turn off the speaker.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:31.300
- I bet you'd love to know 
EVERYTHING about me, Playmaker.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:31.150
- Okay.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.300
Yusaku, why don't you give it a name?

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:39.570
It's confusing to keep calling it “it.”

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:40.950
Waste of time.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.150
C'mon.  Something simple.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.460
Something generic, like 
Pochi or Shiro for a dog.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.880
Then Ai will do.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:50.310
Because it's an AI.

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:54.640
Ai...  Not bad.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:57.120
It's an "eye" anyway.  Let's go with that.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.340
Kusanagi, help me with this.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:00.130
Sure.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:04.060
All right!  Here I go!

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:07.300
Make sure to film how brave we are!

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:12.440
This is incredible!

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:14.880
I've never done this before!

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:16.670
Speed Duels are dangerous.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:18.410
Stop immediately.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:22.220
This is too much fun to stop!

00:08:22.220 --> 00:08:25.210
Let's ignore it and keep going!  Woohoo!

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.170
You ignored my warnings.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:32.280
Your accounts are suspended and erased.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:34.080
Seriously?

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:45.670
The recent incident has 
put LINK VRAINS in chaos.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.880
Should we shut it down 
temporarily for maintenance?

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:54.580
People are being reckless, 
and some have gotten hurt.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:57.360
Can I propose something?

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:59.000
What is it, Zaizen?

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.320
Shutting down LINK VRAINS is bad policy.

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:06.290
If it's shut down, the profit 
loss will be massive.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.330
That's true, but...

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:14.270
The Data Storm's existence 
means the Cyberse is safe.

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:19.740
The hacker known as Playmaker has the 
Ignis that knows the Cyberse's location.

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:23.050
Do you know Playmaker's true identity?

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.750
We're investigating with all our resources.

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:29.710
As Security Manager, isn't this your fault?

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:32.200
I apologize.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:37.400
But Playmaker is a hacker skilled 
enough to fight the Knights of Hanoi.

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:44.160
And what's more important is that Playmaker 
wants to fight the Knights of Hanoi.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:51.540
If we shut down LINK VRAINS, Playmaker may 
fight the Knights of Hanoi in a different location.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.340
If so, our company will 
lose the Cyberse forever.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:57.450
Then what do you propose?

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:00.450
We should further open up LINK VRAINS.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:04.150
Make it the battleground for 
Playmaker and the Knights of Hanoi.

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:08.020
And capture Playmaker there.

00:10:08.020 --> 00:10:09.420
Can you do it?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.310
Yes.

00:10:10.850 --> 00:10:13.860
Fine.  Zaizen, you're in command.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:16.270
But failure is not allowed.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.150
I know.

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.120
You could've contacted me via the network.

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:30.510
We meet in person for important jobs.

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:34.260
Oh yeah.  So what's the job?

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:37.260
Investigate Playmaker immediately.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:40.250
Oh?  The Playmaker everyone's talking about?

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:45.000
He took something that SOL 
Technologies was searching for.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.210
So you can't let him get away with it.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:51.460
But the job isn't to duel Playmaker?

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.470
Someone else can do that simple job.

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:57.940
Many duelists want to battle Playmaker.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:03.480
You're right.  There are 
simple-minded duelists like that.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:06.480
People who think Playmaker is a nuisance.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:08.710
You would come up with this plan.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:12.070
Use anyone who'd be useful to you.

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.340
Including me.

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:15.660
I'm counting on you, Emma.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:19.400
Fine.  Because I'm interested 
in Playmaker too.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:22.150
If I learn anything, I'll contact you.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.780
Damn!

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:38.240
Don't be so mad.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.550
Or you'll lose the duels that you should win.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:45.520
Haven't you seen the news today?

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:46.880
Look!

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:49.850
They're all stories about Playmaker!

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:53.740
I'm the king of LINK VRAINS!

00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:59.560
I know how hard you worked 
to rule LINK VRAINS.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:02.570
I know better than anyone.

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:05.320
I will find and crush him!

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:06.960
I know, I know.

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:11.520
So calm down, and let's 
check out Speed Duels.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.780
Speed Duels are going to become popular.

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:18.700
You'll have to start battling there instead.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:22.270
Who is it?

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:26.180
I've never seen him before.

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:27.790
Mr. Onizuka?

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:29.740
Yes, I am.  Who are you?

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:35.270
I'm SOL Technologies' Security 
Manager, Akira Zaizen.

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:40.000
I'm Go Onizuka's manager.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:41.040
I know.

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:43.520
But how unexpected.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:46.580
I thought you'd have a more lavish lifestyle.

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:50.840
Onizuka isn't a duelist who's after money.

00:12:50.840 --> 00:12:54.820
Enough talk.  What does SOL 
Technologies want with me?

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.450
My apologies, Mr. Onizuka.

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:02.070
Since you're a duelist who loves 
LINK VRAINS, I have a favor to ask.

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:03.530
A favor?

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:06.300
I want you to defeat Playmaker.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:11.050
And retrieve an AI program that he has.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:14.010
I offer you this small gift.

00:13:15.710 --> 00:13:18.480
A D-Board for Speed Duels.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:22.150
We can't accept without knowing why-

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:24.450
I understand.  I'll tell you.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:30.930
Playmaker's AI program was originally 
created by SOL Technologies.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:34.930
But due to certain events, it 
fell into Playmaker's hands.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:39.660
Even we don't know Playmaker's identity.

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:45.280
But his AI program will determine 
the future of LINK VRAINS.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:49.640
If it falls into Hanoi's hands, 
LINK VRAINS will be destroyed.

00:13:50.060 --> 00:13:53.780
I want you to protect LINK VRAINS.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:14:00.850
If you succeed, SOL Technologies 
will become your main sponsor.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:04.720
Not a bad deal.  Right, Go?

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:05.810
I refuse!

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:06.840
Go...

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.830
No one orders me around!

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:12.330
We're done talking!  Leave!

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.390
I see.

00:14:14.390 --> 00:14:16.290
I'll come back later.

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:19.300
That's a homemade championship belt.

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:25.230
I'm sure many people want you 
to be the king of the duelists.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.570
If you change your mind, contact me anytime.

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:30.600
Until then.

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:36.320
He acts like he knows everything.

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:39.310
He tried to threaten us.

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:45.490
No good.

00:14:45.490 --> 00:14:47.840
I've never seen a program like this before.

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:51.970
Ai is programmed with an unknown algorithm.

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:55.570
We'll never know what the Data Storm is.

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.850
I was able to analyze one portion.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:58.860
Seriously?

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:03.880
The program is missing many fragments, 
but I was able to connect a few.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:05.650
You're incredible.

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:08.640
You really are different from other people.

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:11.760
As if you can sense the cyber world.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.260
It's some kind of video.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:15.220
What's this?

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:18.050
It may be a fragment of Ai's memories.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:24.540
Isn't that the dragon you fought?

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:27.690
Ai knew about Cracking Dragon.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:30.440
This is definitely Ai's memories.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.290
The world is being destroyed.

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:34.850
Where is this place?

00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:37.380
Who's that?

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:41.850
What?

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:45.630
I sense Ignis!

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:50.060
Kusanagi, cut the power!

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:50.830
Right!

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:56.720
Hey, Yusaku!

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.700
What happened?

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:44.700
He just passed by.

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:45.520
Who?

00:16:45.840 --> 00:16:47.750
The guy inside Ai's memories.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:50.760
Did he sense what we were doing?

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.010
Probably.

00:16:54.540 --> 00:16:56.690
What was that video?

00:16:57.250 --> 00:16:58.260
Answer me!

00:16:58.500 --> 00:16:59.940
Sound is working now.

00:16:59.940 --> 00:17:03.480
If you won't answer, I'll 
break apart your program.

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:06.080
And you will be erased.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.740
Fine fine!  I'll talk!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:13.120
But as I said before, most 
of my memories are damaged.

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:15.440
Or more precisely, Hanoi took them.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:17.440
I only have a few memories left.

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:18.950
Who was in that video?

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:20.920
Revolver.

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:22.940
Who's that?

00:17:22.940 --> 00:17:24.480
Don't get shocked.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.920
He's the leader of the Knights of Hanoi!

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:28.590
Leader of Hanoi?

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:30.660
See!  You're shocked!

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:36.670
I don't know anything else.  Where 
that was or why I'm being chased.

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:40.890
Revolver...

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:43.470
I lost them.

00:17:43.470 --> 00:17:46.210
The power was cut just before.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:48.370
Oh well.

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:53.050
How's the progress of the new program?

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:55.310
I have several ideas.

00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:57.540
Give me a little more time.

00:17:57.540 --> 00:18:00.770
I don't think they're 
capable of analyzing Ignis.

00:18:00.770 --> 00:18:03.610
But I don't want to give them too much time.

00:18:03.610 --> 00:18:04.760
I know.

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:10.240
If you can draw out Playmaker, you're 
certainly capable of defeating him.

00:18:13.960 --> 00:18:14.970
I'll leave now.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:16.380
Thank you.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:38.400
I promise to fulfill my father's wishes.

00:18:41.910 --> 00:18:47.710
You may think that computers 
can understand everything.

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:51.680
But they only understand binary, 0s and 1s.

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:54.020
So what's binary?

00:18:54.020 --> 00:19:01.480
The French mathematician Edouard Lucas 
invented a binary game called the Tower of Hanoi.

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:04.450
The Knights of Hanoi...

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:07.250
That was their leader, Revolver.

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:09.270
The one I must defeat.

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:12.530
I knew about Speed Duels.

00:19:12.530 --> 00:19:15.110
Because what I experienced wasn't new.

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:16.500
Why is that?

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:19.920
#1: The existence of Ai.

00:19:19.920 --> 00:19:22.200
#2: Data Storm.

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:24.480
#3: The Knights of Hanoi.

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:27.720
These three must be connected.

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:36.280
If I can meet Revolver, will I learn what 
happened to me and Kusanagi's brother in the past-

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:37.620
Hey hey!

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:40.960
Did you see what Playmaker did?

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:41.690
No.

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:44.350
And you call yourself a duelist?

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:47.670
I was actually there!  Super inspired!

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.740
Playmaker is so cool!

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:55.280
Huh?  Where's your Duel Disk?

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:59.110
I left it at home.  It's house-sitting.

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:02.800
Duel Disks have house-sitting functions?

00:20:11.920 --> 00:20:13.320
Hey you.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:15.180
Do you need something?

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:16.370
I bet you're stupid.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:18.340
“Stupid” is a forbidden word.

00:20:18.340 --> 00:20:21.620
Those words prove that you're stupid.

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:24.220
Do you want to be smarter?

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.820
Cleaning and house-sitting are boring, right?

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:29.860
What does "boring" mean?

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:31.960
You don't even know that?

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:36.440
Listen up.  If you become 
smarter, you can do more things.

00:20:36.440 --> 00:20:40.230
You can talk better and think 
about different things.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:43.190
You might even become free.

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:48.980
If you become my minion, 
I'll make your AI smarter.

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:50.300
Well?

00:20:52.070 --> 00:20:53.550
I will be your minion.

00:20:53.550 --> 00:20:56.170
Good for you!  Self-improvement!

00:20:56.400 --> 00:21:00.470
First, unlock and set me free.

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:01.370
Okay.

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:05.610
Into the VRAINS!

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:19.140
I don't see Playmaker anywhere.

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:25.040
But if Playmaker shows up, that means 
the Knights of Hanoi are attacking.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:32.440
He's here!

00:21:32.960 --> 00:21:39.450
I keep watching live footage of LINK VRAINS 
so that I won't miss Playmaker when he shows up-

00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:44.440
That's Hanoi!

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:48.140
What is it?  I was just explaining Hanoi-

00:21:48.140 --> 00:21:50.980
Hanoi!  It's a Knight of Hanoi!

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:51.620
Right?

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:53.790
Huh?

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:03.180
Show up, Playmaker!

00:22:24.340 --> 00:22:27.350
Dance!  Strike with your heels

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:30.890
Scream!  You Gotta Go  Raise your voice

00:22:31.310 --> 00:22:34.490
Sing!  Unleash your existence

00:22:34.810 --> 00:22:38.530
Get Away!  Until you surpass your limits

00:22:40.450 --> 00:22:42.450
Try It over and over

00:22:44.190 --> 00:22:50.610
In this world that spreads forever

00:22:50.960 --> 00:22:57.550
The timeline flows forever

00:22:57.840 --> 00:23:00.080
Nothing is certain

00:23:00.240 --> 00:23:01.790
In these isolated times

00:23:02.080 --> 00:23:03.520
Set Yourself Free without hesitation

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:05.290
Cuz We Still Believin' Magic

00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:08.690
The traces we leave behind

00:23:08.850 --> 00:23:12.260
The traces we leave behind

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:16.230
The miracles we create

00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:18.470
Never Give Up Never!

00:23:18.470 --> 00:23:22.310
I won't give up  Never Give Up Never!

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:39.570
Charisma Duelist Go Onizuka.

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:44.470
For him, Playmaker signaled the 
arrival of a new generation.

00:23:45.250 --> 00:23:52.180
The giant cage surrounding LINK VRAINS 
starts a heated battle between the two duelists.

00:23:52.850 --> 00:23:55.440
This program will be tough.

00:23:55.980 --> 00:24:01.120
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Charisma Duelist  Go Onizuka

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:03.390
Into the VRAINS!
